  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "I really think it would be great to see an optional toggle on the avatar descriptor or a new component to synchronize avatar physics. I have seen as well as made quite a few avatars that have made heavy use of rigidbodies and joints which work properly for the user but can sometimes break for others from something as simple as moving or respawning. Additionally, rather than just synchronizing the physics, you could possibly implement something similar to networked IK (except please don't break it like you did with IK) where your client sends the transforms of the physics objects every x milliseconds to everyone else  to make physics better on performance too.",
